Description: CI diagnostic: report why linkAnnex failed
 The nightly `test-annex (nfs-home)` job intermittently fails with
 "<file> failed to link to annex" (git-annex add of an unlocked file) or
 "unlock failed", in a different test each night.  Both messages come
 from linkAnnex returning LinkAnnexFailed, which is reachable by two
 paths that say nothing at all about what went wrong:
 .
  * linkOrCopy returned Nothing - either an IOException was swallowed by
    catchDefaultIO/catchBoolIO, or cp / the chmod in preserveGitMode
    returned False;
  * the source file's inode cache (inode, size, high resolution mtime)
    did not compare equal before and after the copy, so checksrcunchanged
    deleted the destination.
 .
 The CI transcripts cannot distinguish these, which makes the NFS
 failures impossible to diagnose after the fact.  This patch adds a
 warning to each of those paths, including the before/after inode caches,
 so that the next failing run says which one it is.
 .
 Diagnostic only - no behaviour change beyond the extra messages on
 paths that already fail.  Drop it once the cause is understood.
 .
 Drafted with Claude Code assistance.
